# 16 — Markdown Structure

Every markdown file you create or modify must have reasonable paragraph breaks and correct, logical headings. This applies whether the file is written for humans or agents.

Split long paragraphs where the topic changes. Use one `#` title, then nest heading levels in order without skipping a level. Each heading must accurately name the content under it. When you fix breaks or headings, keep the meaning of the text unchanged.
